OL,3,AKidnapper, 74, escapes from house
OL,4,Aarrest in Argentina by abseiling from
OL,5,Abalcony
OL,6,
OL,7,FA 74-year-old Italian man who was found
OL,8,Fguilty of a kidnapping carried out by a
OL,9,Ffar-left militant group in the 1970s
OL,10,Fhas escaped while under house arrest in
OL,11,FArgentina and is on the run.
OL,13,FLeonardo Bertulazzi used a harness to
OL,14,Fabseil down from a fifth-floor balcony
OL,15,Fin the capital, Buenos Aires.
OL,17,FHis escape was not immediately
OL,18,Fregistered because he had tampered with
OL,19,Fhis electronic ankle monitor so that it
OL,20,Fcontinued to transmit body temperature
OL,21,Fmeasurements even after he had prised
OL,22,Fit open and absconded.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,317,300,200,140,0,100
